{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/SsfReceiver"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Poll the stream’s RFC 8936 endpoint, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{base URL}\/ssf\/v1\/poll\/{stream_id}"},{"type":"text","text":", with a bearer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the configured "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/SsfReceiverConfiguration\/accessTokenProvider"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK11SsfReceiverC4poll8streamID7optionsAA0C10PollResultVSS_AA0cI7OptionsVtYaKF","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","title":"poll(streamID:options:)","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"poll","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"streamID","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"options","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK14SsfPollOptionsV","text":"SsfPollOptions"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK13SsfPollResultV","text":"SsfPollResult"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"poll","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"streamID","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"options","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SsfPollOptions","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK14SsfPollOptionsV","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/SsfPollOptions"},{"text":" = SsfPollOptions()) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SsfPollResult","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK13SsfPollResultV","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/SsfPollResult"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ack"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setErrs"},{"type":"text","text":" are sent exactly as given. "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Nothing is acknowledged on your","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"behalf","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": acknowledge, on the next call, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"jti"},{"type":"text","text":"s you processed, and pass each refused"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setErrs"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SetErr(reason:)"},{"type":"text","text":"). A SET you neither acknowledge nor refuse is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"re-offered — and, having been recorded when it verified, then reads as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"replayed"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Retried per §16 on a transport failure, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"408"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"429"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"5xx"},{"type":"text","text":"; never on another "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"4xx"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which maps as the management surface maps it ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"400"},{"type":"text","text":" is a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/NetworkError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/NetworkError\/isValidation","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" set, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"404"},{"type":"text","text":" an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthzError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"…)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A failure that is not a verdict never costs an event"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (CONTRACT.md §34.2 P1). A key"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fetch that fails, or a replay store that cannot answer, stops the batch at that SET:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the SETs already verified are returned in "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/SsfPollResult\/events","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (they are recorded),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and that SET and every later one are listed in "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/SsfPollResult\/unjudged","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unrecorded, neither acknowledge nor refuse them, and the transmitter offers them again."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"When no SET of the batch was accepted, nothing is recorded and the failure is thrown"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instead. A SET refused "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"replayed"},{"type":"text","text":" was accepted by this receiver earlier: acknowledge it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ack"},{"type":"text","text":" rather than reporting it in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setErrs"},{"type":"text","text":" (§34.2 P2). A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"poll"},{"type":"text","text":" that returns leaving"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SETs unjudged emits "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/TelemetryEvent\/ssfUnjudged(operation:count:category:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (§19.1)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Throws","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A local "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" when no access-token provider is configured."}]}],"type":"aside"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/ssfreceiver\/poll(streamid:options:)"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/SsfReceiver\/poll(streamID:options:)"},"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/SsfReceiver":{"title":"SsfReceiver","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/ssfreceiver","fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SsfReceiver","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The SSF receiver helper (CONTRACT.md §32.7) — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verifySet"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"poll"},{"type":"text","text":" over a receiver"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"configuration."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SsfReceiver","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/SsfReceiver"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/AuthzError":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Au